-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the calculus, as a table
-- what an eliminator does with a value: a body to build with the eliminator's wires innermost
-- (act-ap), or with the value's parts innermost, the last part first (act-rp), or with the value
-- itself innermost and then the eliminator's wires (act-self), a value outright, nothing, or
-- (act-stuck) the eliminator kept as it is, holding the value: an operation the machine does not
-- compute, read back whole and computed on bodies
data NkAct = act-ap (t : NkTm) | act-rp (t : NkTm) | act-self (t : NkTm) | act-hd (h : NkHd) | act-none | act-stuck
